@startuml SD-004: Task Delegation Chain
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title SD-004: Task Delegation Chain (default OOAD workflow v2.0.0)
subtitle Each agent hands its output to the next through workflow variables

actor "Board Member" as User #LightBlue
participant "WorkflowEngine" as Engine #Orange
participant "AgentOrchestrator\n(IAgent[] from AGENTS)" as Orch #Orange
participant "CEO" as CEO #Pink
participant "BA" as BA #LightGreen
participant "Architect" as Architect #LightGreen
participant "OOAD Gate\n(QualityGateStrategy)" as Gate #Yellow
participant "PM" as PM #Pink
participant "DEV" as DEV #LightGreen
participant "QC" as QC #LightGreen
participant "QA" as QA #LightGreen
participant "Marketing" as MKT #LightGreen
database "ProjectWorkspace\nprojects/<id>/" as WS #LightGray
database "PrismaDB" as DB #LightGray

note over Engine, Orch
  **Hand-off mechanism**: every agent_task node calls
  orchestrator.invokeAgent(role, context). The strategy's typed output
  (BaOutput, QcOutput, ...) is merged into the run's variables, so the next
  agent and the condition nodes read it (code, qcReport, qa_approved).
  Agents never call each other directly.
end note

User -> Engine: startWorkflow(projectId, 'default-project-workflow')
activate Engine
Engine -> DB: workflowRun.create({status: 'running', currentNodeId: 'start'})

== Analysis ==

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('CEO', {taskType: 'planMilestones', goal})
Orch -> CEO: execute(context)
CEO --> Orch: CeoOutput { action: 'planMilestones', output }
Orch --> Engine: result
Engine -> DB: milestone.create(...) (one per listed milestone)

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('BA', {taskType: 'generateUseCases'})
Orch -> BA: execute(context)
BA -> WS: docs/use-cases.md, docs/use-case-diagram.puml
BA -> DB: project.ooadMetadata.useCases
BA --> Orch: BaOutput { useCases, actors, filesWritten }
Orch --> Engine: result

== Design ==

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('ARCHITECT', {taskType: 'designArchitecture'})
Orch -> Architect: execute(context)
Architect -> DB: read ooadMetadata.useCases
Architect -> WS: domain-model.puml, class-diagram.puml, sequence-UC-xxx.puml,\narchitecture-patterns.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, src/** skeleton
Architect -> DB: ooadMetadata.{domainModel, patterns, architecture}
Architect --> Orch: ArchitectOutput { domainModel, patterns, skeletonFiles }
Orch --> Engine: result

Engine -> Gate: execute('ooad_gate', criteria)
Gate -> DB: counts (use cases ≥ 5, entities ≥ 3, patterns ≥ 3)
Gate -> WS: required artifacts exist?
alt gate failed
  Gate --> Engine: onFail
  Engine -> Architect: back to 'design' (redesign)
else gate passed
  Gate --> Engine: onSuccess
end

== Implementation ==

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('PM', {taskType: 'breakdownTasks'})
Orch -> PM: execute(context)
PM -> DB: read approved use cases
PM --> Orch: PmOutput { output: '1. UC-001 ...' }
Orch --> Engine: result
Engine -> DB: task.create(...) (one per use case, status todo)

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('DEV', {taskType: 'implement'})
Orch -> DEV: execute(context + OOAD design)
DEV -> WS: src/** (paths normalised, traversal rejected)
DEV --> Orch: DevOutput { code, filesWritten }
Orch --> Engine: result
Engine -> DB: tasks todo/in_progress → review

== Verification ==

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('QC', {taskType: 'verify'})
Orch -> QC: execute(context)
QC -> WS: tests/UC-xxx.spec.ts
participant "SandboxExecutor\n(runInWorkspace)" as Sandbox #LightYellow
QC -> Sandbox: jest --json on projects/<id> (read-only mount, no network)
Sandbox --> QC: Jest report → JestReportMapper (per UC-xxx)
QC -> WS: docs/traceability-matrix.md (Passing / Failing / Missing)
QC -> DB: ooadMetadata.{testCoverage, traceability (pass/fail counts)}
QC --> Orch: QcOutput { qc_passed, testCoverage, failingTests, qcReport }
Orch --> Engine: result

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('QA', {taskType: 'review', code, qcReport, failingTests})
Orch -> QA: execute(context)
QA --> Orch: QaOutput { qa_approved }
Orch --> Engine: result

alt qa_approved = false
  Engine -> DB: review tasks → in_progress
  Engine -> DEV: back to 'develop' (fix findings)
else qa_approved = true
  Engine -> DB: review tasks → done
end

== Release ==

Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('MARKETING', {taskType: 'draftAnnouncement'})
Orch -> MKT: execute(context)
MKT --> Orch: MarketingOutput { output }
Orch --> Engine: result

Engine -> User: human_approval ('project_completion')
User --> Engine: approve
Engine -> Orch: invokeAgent('CEO', {taskType: 'complete_project'})
Orch -> CEO: execute(context)
CEO --> Orch: CeoOutput { action: 'complete_project', output: close-out report }
Engine -> DB: workflowRun.update({status: 'completed'})
Engine --> User: WorkflowCompleted
deactivate Engine

note over User, DB
  **Chain**: CEO → BA → Architect → [OOAD gate] → PM → DEV → QC → QA → [qa_approved] → Marketing → [approval] → CEO
  Backward edges: gate fail → Architect, QA reject → DEV.
  QC (product: tests, traceability) and QA (process: design conformance) form a review chain.
end note

@enduml
